{
  "requirement": "The source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.\n\n```rust,ignore\nlet file = std::path::PathBuf::from(\"src/auth.rs\");\n```\n\nAn item within that file uses the path and selector in `OutlineId` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict.** The reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.sources.source_addresses`. Its text imposes two obligations. I judged them against the public `Sources` API in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/source_defaults.rs`, which uses `PathBuf` addresses.\n\n**Obligation 1: source tools identify project files with project-relative `PathBuf` values.**\n- `fn[gitignore_is_shared_by_all_operations_with_or_without_a_git_repository]` builds `Sources` on an absolute tempdir root. It asserts that `list` returns relative paths such as `keep.txt`, `src/nested.txt` and `.visible`, and it passes a relative `PathBuf` to `read` and `parse`. It also asserts that `search_text` reports `matches[0].path == Path::new(\"src/nested.txt\")`, scoped through the prefix `./src/../src`.\n- `fn[scoped_inspection_skips_unrelated_directories_and_reports_relevant_ignore_errors]` asserts `listed[0] == Path::new(\"src/one.txt\")`.\n- `fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` shows addresses are relative to the project root and not valid outside it. `read` fails for `../outside.txt`, for `../note.txt` as a `PathBuf`, for an absolute path to an existing file, and for a missing file. It also asserts `parsed.id().path == Path::new(\"note.txt\")`.\n- `fn[built_in_languages_and_structural_search_use_the_project_scope]` asserts that structural matches carry the relative `node.path`, `visible.rs`. It also checks that a `..` prefix is rejected.\n\n**Obligation 2: an item within a file uses the path and selector of `OutlineId`.**\n- This obligation is governed by `requirements.sdk.outlines.address_identity`, which the subject cites. Under the task rules, a cited requirement is context and its implementation and tests are not reassessed.\n- The tests still cover its application here. `fn[empty_sources_errors_and_retained_snapshots_remain_distinct]` asserts that a parsed whole-file snapshot has `id().path` equal to the relative path and an empty `selector`. `fn[outline_addresses_validate_selectors_without_reading_paths]` in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/search.rs` constructs `OutlineId::new(path, selector)` with an opaque `PathBuf`. It keeps the path and selector unchanged and rejects malformed selectors.\n\n**Additional tests.** `src/sources/tests.rs` has `fn[local_provider_scopes_paths_and_rejects_resources_outside_its_root]` and `fn[addresses_preserve_opaque_fields_and_compare_each_identity_component]`. They exercise the internal `ResourceId` and `resource::OutlineId` types, not the public `PathBuf` contract. They add only some extra coverage and don't weaken it. The first rejects outside-root resources, `..` prefixes, absolute locations and symlink escapes. The second checks that each identity component affects equality.\n\n**Gaps.** I found no unaddressed obligation or untested boundary, and no applicable `{fixme}`.",
  "references": "df11f66fd68a124ab40cef9071bf3bccaac4decfa892b3cefd1b981b483de25d",
